<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saint David</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 589</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Dewi Sant</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a>, Dewi Sant in Welsh, was a 6th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> and monastic founder in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> and is the patron saint of Wales. His monastery at Mynyw, later St Davids, became the leading church of Wales and a major place of pilgrimage. His feast day, 1 March, is the national day of Wales.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saint-david.jpg" alt="Saint David" width="320" height="531" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hchc2009 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Castell_Coch_stained_glass_panel_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
